                <pb facs="0531" n="521" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg521"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.796/365: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-05-16T16:00:00-03:00">May 16, 1941—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>480. Department’s telegram No. 292, May 12, 10 p.m. Aranha promises me that
                    Lufthansa will not be allowed to resume trans-Atlantic operations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
